Hello Omar,

On your Enterprise plan, the REST API limit is 3,000 requests per minute. When this limit is
exceeded, the API returns a 429 status code along with a Retry-After header that specifies how
many seconds to wait before retrying.

To help prevent hitting this limit, you can use our bulk endpoints, which accept up to 100 records
per call and count as a single request, and make sure your sync honors the Retry-After header. You
can find more details in article KB-602.

Please let us know if you have any other questions.

Daniel Okafor

